# Two inks.
#
# Desaturate, then map the greyscale onto a ramp between two colours. Because
# the mapping is by brightness, the dark ink lands in the shadows and the pale
# one in the highlights, and the picture keeps its tonal structure while losing
# its own colour entirely.
#
# Defaults are a navy and a warm paper. Any two colours work, but the pair
# wants a real difference in lightness or the result flattens to a single wash.

param dark = #1b2a4a
param light = #f2e4c9

adjust black-and-white
adjust levels black=0.03 white=0.97
adjust gradient-map from={dark} to={light}
